  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "S1",
      "obj_id": "S-1",
      "kind": "setup",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "A latent causal model on \\(n\\) scalar variables. Fix \\(n\\in\\mathbb N\\), the labeled vertex set \\([n]=\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}\\), a finite labeled directed acyclic graph \\(G\\) on \\([n]\\) with parent sets \\(\\operatorname{pa}_G(i)\\), and a sign vector \\(s\\in\\{-1,+1\\}^n\\). The latent state is \\(V=(V_1,\\ldots,V_n)\\in[0,1]^n\\). A mechanism is a pair of families \\(((p_i,q_i))_{i=1}^n\\) in which \\(p_i:[0,1]^{1+|\\operatorname{pa}_G(i)|}\\to(0,\\infty)\\) is the observational conditional density of \\(V_i\\) given \\(V_{\\operatorname{pa}_G(i)}\\) and \\(q_i:[0,1]\\to(0,\\infty)\\) is the parent-independent perfect-intervention density at target \\(i\\), with distribution function \\(Q_i(v)=\\int_0^v q_i(u)\\,du\\). The observational latent law is \\(p^0(v)=\\prod_{i=1}^n p_i(v_i\\mid v_{\\operatorname{pa}_G(i)})\\) and the target-\\(i\\) interventional latent law is \\(p^i(v)=q_i(v_i)\\prod_{\\ell\\ne i}p_\\ell(v_\\ell\\mid v_{\\operatorname{pa}_G(\\ell)})\\). Write \\(j\\lessdot_G i\\) when \\(j\\) is a strict ancestor of \\(i\\) in \\(G\\) with no vertex strictly between them in the ancestral order. The model stratum \\(\\Theta_{G,s}\\) is the set of mechanisms that are positive, normalized, \\(C^3\\), causally minimal for \\(G\\), and of prescribed own-coordinate log-ratio derivative signs \\(s\\), carrying the relative product \\(C^2\\) topology. Three distinguished points of this world are the sparse witness \\(\\theta^{\\mathrm{sp}}\\), the cancellation witness \\(\\theta^{\\mathrm{can}}\\), and the nodewise normalized affine path \\(\\theta^t\\), \\(t\\in[0,1]\\), interpolating a mechanism toward \\(\\theta^{\\mathrm{sp}}\\). — Reused graph primitive: `Causalean.DAG` on `Fin n` (Causalean/Graph/DAG.lean:57), with `Causalean.DAG.parents`, `Causalean.DAG.isAncestor`, `Causalean.DAG.isAncestor_trans`, `Causalean.DAG.ancestors`, `Causalean.DAG.topoOrder`, `Causalean.DAG.isAncestor_topoOrder_lt`. The ancestral cover relation \\(j\\lessdot_G i\\) is `CovBy` (Mathlib.Order.Defs.PartialOrder / Mathlib.Order.Cover) for the strict order induced by `DAG.isAncestor`; the note's `an ancestral cover in a DAG is a directed edge` step is then `CovBy` unfolded against `DAG.isAncestor_child`. Mechanisms are `ContDiffOn ℝ 3` positive normalized densities on closed cubes; the relative product \\(C^2\\) topology is the sup-norm-through-order-two topology on the finite product of mechanism slots, defined locally. Search trace: grep `Diffeomorph|diffeomorph|mixing map|unmixing|latent representation` over ../Causalean → 0 files; API.md §1 (Graph/DAG), §6 (SCM/Model/SCM), §9 (SCM/ID/Identifiable), §8h (PO/) read — no mechanism-stratum or density-family primitive; Mathlib side lean_leansearch `continuously differentiable function ContDiff definition` → `ContDiff`/`ContDiffOn` in Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.ContDiff.Defs (reused), no causal-mechanism stratum. Bypass-justified over Mathlib for everything except the DAG.",
        "tex_anchor": "",
        "frozen": true
