    {
      "id": "S2",
      "obj_id": "S-2",
      "kind": "setup",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "The observed environment family generated by a shared mixing map. Let \\(f:[0,1]^n\\to\\mathcal X\\) be a \\(C^2\\) diffeomorphism onto the observed support \\(\\mathcal X\\), the same map in every environment, and let \\(X=f(V)\\) be the observation. For \\(e=0\\) the observed law \\(P^e\\) is the pushforward of \\(p^0\\) under \\(f\\); for \\(e\\in[n]\\) it is the pushforward of \\(p^{\\pi(e)}\\), where \\(\\pi\\) is an unknown bijection from interventional environment labels to latent intervention targets. The environment-label DAG \\(G^\\pi\\) is the pullback of \\(G\\) by \\(\\pi\\): \\(j\\to i\\) in \\(G^\\pi\\) exactly when \\(\\pi(j)\\to\\pi(i)\\) in \\(G\\). The observable invariants are the density ratios \\(R_i=dP^i/dP^0:\\mathcal X\\to(0,\\infty)\\), which after unmixing equal \\(q_{\\pi(i)}(v_{\\pi(i)})/p_{\\pi(i)}(v_{\\pi(i)}\\mid v_{\\operatorname{pa}_G(\\pi(i))})\\), together with their logarithms \\(L_i=\\log R_i\\). — bypass-justified: no Causalean module models a latent-to-observed mixing map or an environment family indexed by unknown intervention targets (grep `Diffeomorph|mixing map|unmixing` over ../Causalean → 0 files; API.md §8h PO/, §6b SCM/Model/Kernel, §9 SCM/ID all condition on observed variables with a known diagram). Built over `MeasureTheory.Measure.map` (Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Map, verified) for \\(P^e\\) and `ContDiffOn ℝ 2` plus an explicit two-sided inverse for the diffeomorphism; \\(\\pi\\) is an `Equiv.Perm (Fin n)`; \\(G^\\pi\\) is `Causalean.DAG` transported along that permutation. The proofs use \\(R_i\\) only through its unmixed latent form \\(r_i(v)=q_i(v_i)/p_i(v_i\\mid v_{\\operatorname{pa}_G(i)})\\), so the Jacobian cancellation is a single change-of-variables lemma in this S-block.",
        "tex_anchor": "",
        "frozen": true
      },
      "lean": {
