    {
      "id": "S4",
      "obj_id": "S-4",
      "kind": "setup",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "The population decoder. Fix a topological ordering of \\(H_D\\) and let \\(B_i\\subseteq[n]\\) be the environment labels preceding \\(i\\) in it. Let \\(C_i(t\\mid\\ell_{B_i})=P^i(L_i\\le t\\mid L_{B_i}=\\ell_{B_i})\\), taken in its continuous version on the model support, and let \\(U_i(x)=C_i(L_i(x)\\mid L_{B_i}(x))\\) be the identified rank coordinate. The population recovery map \\(\\mathscr D\\) sends \\((P^0,\\ldots,P^n)\\) to \\((H_D,(U_i)_{i=1}^n,G^\\pi)\\): it forms every \\(R_i\\) and \\(D_{ji}\\), builds \\(H_D\\), selects a topological ordering, constructs every \\(U_i\\), aligns environment \\(i\\) with \\(U_i\\), and at each \\(i\\) returns as parent set the unique inclusion-minimal \\(A\\subseteq B_i\\) with \\(U_i\\mathbin{\\perp\\!\\!\\!\\perp}_{P^0}U_{B_i\\setminus A}\\mid U_A\\). — bypass-justified: Causalean's decoding layer (`SCM.ID.Identifiable`, `GraphicalThms.*`, `Graph.MarkovEquiv.*`) decides identifiability of a functional under a KNOWN diagram or Markov-equivalence of two GIVEN DAGs; none of them constructs a graph from a family of environment laws. Search trace: grep `populationDecoder|decoder|rank coordinate|parent pruning` over ../Causalean → no match; API.md §4b (MarkovEquiv), §9 (SCM/ID), §8d (Global Markov) read — recovery direction absent. Mathlib side lean_leansearch `conditional distribution condDistrib regular conditional probability` → `ProbabilityTheory.condDistrib` (Mathlib.Probability.Kernel.CondDistrib, verified) supplies \\(C_i\\); the note's own equation (11) gives the explicit continuous version \\(C_i(t\\mid\\ell_{B_i})=\\int_0^1\\mathbf 1\\{\\lambda_i(w,v_{\\operatorname{pa}}) \\le t\\}q_i(w)\\,dw\\), so F2 should DEFINE \\(C_i\\) by that integral and prove it agrees with `condDistrib`, rather than fight a.e.-versions. Conditional independence reuses `Causalean.Mathlib.CondIndep` (Causalean/Mathlib/CondIndep.lean) re-exports of `ProbabilityTheory.CondIndepFun`. Round-5 correction (decision P-D11) on the weak-union step (15): the round-4 `Causalean.SCM.Do.obsCondIndep_weak_union` claim is WITHDRAWN and `Causalean.SCM.Do.SemiGraphoid` is wholly `bypass-justified`. That declaration (SemiGraphoid.lean:249, signature re-read 2026-09-06: `(M : Causalean.SCM N Ω) [StandardBorelSpace M.ObservedValues] {X Y W Z : Finset (SWIGNode N)} (hX : X ⊆ M.observed) (hYW : (Y ∪ W) ⊆ M.observed) (hZ : Z ⊆ M.observed) {μ} [IsFiniteMeasure μ] (h : ObsCondIndep M X (Y ∪ W) Z …) : ObsCondIndep M X Y (Z ∪ W) …`) requires a `Causalean.SCM N Ω`, SWIG-node `Finset`s, and observed-variable projections, none of which exist in S4: here the coordinates \\(U_i\\), \\(V_i\\), \\(L_i\\) are locally defined rank and log-ratio functions on \\(\\mathcal X\\) under a generic continuous-density law, and the DAG is the latent \\(G\\) being recovered rather than a known diagram, so the SCM/SWIG theorem is not instantiable. Step (15) instead reuses the GENERIC `Causalean.condIndepFun_weak_union_of_prodMk` (Causalean/Mathlib/CondIndep/CondExp.lean:545, `namespace Causalean`, exported by `Causalean.Mathlib.CondIndep`; signature read 2026-09-06: `(hm : m ≤ mΩ) [StandardBorelSpace Ω] {μ} [IsFiniteMeasure μ] {W : Ω → α} {V : Ω → β} {A : Ω → γ} (hW : Measurable W) (hV : Measurable V) (hA : Measurable A) (hCI : CondIndepFun m hm W (fun ω => (V ω, A ω)) μ) : CondIndepFun (m ⊔ MeasurableSpace.comap A inferInstance) (sup_le hm hA.comap_le) W V μ`), instantiated at `W = U_i`, `V = U_b`, `A = U_{(B_i∖A)∖{b}}`, `m = σ(U_A)`. The required measurable coordinate-pair bridge — presenting \\(U_{B_i\\setminus A}\\) as the measurable pair \\((U_b, U_{(B_i\\setminus A)\\setminus\\{b\\}})\\) and identifying `σ(U_A) ⊔ σ(U_{(B_i∖A)∖{b}}) = σ(U_{B_i∖{b}})` — is the small local helper `condIndep_coordSplit_prodMk` (`Helpers/CondIndepIntersection.lean`), which needs only measurability of the finitely many coordinate maps and `MeasurableSpace.comap` algebra. Search trace (round 5): grep `weak_union|weak union` over ../Causalean → `SCM/Do/SemiGraphoid.lean` (SCM/SWIG-typed, not instantiable here) and `Mathlib/CondIndep/CondExp.lean:545` `condIndepFun_weak_union_of_prodMk` (generic, reused); Mathlib side lean_leansearch `conditional independence weak union graphoid property` → `ProbabilityTheory.CondIndepFun` with no graphoid-axiom layer, so the Causalean generic lemma is strictly the better fit. Round-4 correction (decision P-D10) on the INTERSECTION property, which stands: `Causalean/SCM/Do/SemiGraphoid.lean` provides decomposition/weak-union/contraction only — its full declaration list is `ObsCondIndep` (61), `obsCondIndep_symm` (79), `condIndep_valuesProjection_symm` (90), `condIndep_valuesProjection_subset_right` (112), `condIndep_valuesProjection_decomposition` (136), `condIndep_valuesProjection_weak_union_axiom` (159), `condIndep_valuesProjection_contraction_axiom` (185), `obsCondIndep_subset_right` (215), `obsCondIndep_decomposition` (232), `obsCondIndep_weak_union` (249), `obsCondIndep_contraction` (267) — there is no intersection lemma anywhere in it, which is correct, since intersection is the one semi-graphoid property that is NOT an axiom of a general semi-graphoid and needs strict positivity. The proof's steps (16)-(18) are therefore realized by a NEW LOCAL lemma `condIndep_intersection_of_pos` (`Helpers/CondIndepIntersection.lean`), derived from the model's own strict positive-density assumption `ass:positive-normalized-smooth-mechanisms` already in the .tex: the frozen proof of `thm:exact-ratio-decoder` supplies the argument verbatim at equation (17) — the two conditional-density identities, extended from a.e. to everywhere by positivity and continuity, force `p^0(v_i ∣ v_W, v_Z) = p^0(v_i ∣ v_b, v_Z)` to be constant in both \\(v_b\\) and \\(v_W\\) on the full positive product support. Search trace: grep `intersection|Intersection` over ../Causalean/SCM/Do/SemiGraphoid.lean → 0 matches; grep `condIndep.*intersection|semiGraphoid|semi_graphoid` over ../Causalean → no intersection declaration; Mathlib side lean_leansearch `conditional independence intersection property strictly positive density` (run 2026-09-06) → `ProbabilityTheory.CondIndepSets.inter`, `.iInter`, `.bInter`, `condIndepSet_iff`, `cond_iInter` (Mathlib.Probability.Independence.Conditional / .Basic). `CondIndepSets.inter` is a NEAR MISS, not a fit: it intersects two set FAMILIES on one side of a fixed conditional independence, whereas the graphoid intersection property splices two independences with different conditioning sets and is false without positivity. Mathlib has `ProbabilityTheory.CondIndepFun` but no graphoid-axiom layer and no positivity-based intersection lemma.",
