    {
      "id": "S5",
      "obj_id": "S-5",
      "kind": "setup",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "Independent multi-sample sampling with sample splitting. Within each environment \\(e\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n\\}\\) the \\(N_e\\) observations are independent draws from \\(P^e\\), and the training and evaluation folds are independent; \\(\\underline N=\\min_{0\\le e\\le n}N_e\\). On the training folds a density-ratio estimate \\(\\widehat R_i:\\mathcal X\\to(0,\\infty)\\) is fitted without the evaluation observations; \\(a_N\\in[0,\\infty)\\) is a deterministic radius for the joint evaluation-law \\(L^1\\) error of those fitted ratios, holding with probability at least \\(1-\\eta\\). On the independent evaluation folds \\(\\widehat D_{ji}\\) is the norm of the difference of the empirical Gaussian-kernel mean embeddings of \\(\\widehat R_i(X)\\) under environments \\(0\\) and \\(j\\). With familywise level \\(\\alpha\\in(0,1)\\) and first-stage failure level \\(\\eta\\in(0,1)\\), the simultaneous confidence radius is \\(\\varepsilon_N(\\alpha,\\eta)=2\\sqrt2\\,a_N+2[1+\\sqrt{2\\log(n(n+1)/\\alpha)}]/\\sqrt{\\min_e N_e}\\), and the sample-split confidence graph \\(\\widehat H\\) has arrow \\(j\\to i\\) exactly when \\(\\widehat D_{ji}-\\varepsilon_N(\\alpha,\\eta)>0\\). — Round-4 correction (decision P-D9): `Causalean.ML.Kernel.RKHS` is dropped from this S-block too — the empirical mean embedding \\(\\widehat\\mu_{ie}\\) and \\(\\widehat D_{ji}\\) are built from the LOCAL `UnitNormFeatureMap`/`meanEmbedding` layer of S3 (`Helpers/Kernel.lean`), not from `Causalean.ML.IsRKHS`, which supplies only the reproducing identity and no bounded-feature concentration interface. The i.i.d.-within-environment product law is `MeasureTheory.Measure.pi` over `Fin N_e`; the training/evaluation split is expressed by conditioning on the training σ-algebra, exactly as the note does. Reused concentration engine: `mcdiarmid_inequality_pos` (third_party/lean-rademacher/FoML/McDiarmid.lean:937), re-exported by `Causalean.Stat.Concentration.TailBounds.McDiarmid`; its hypotheses `iIndepFun X μ` and `|f x - f (Function.update x i x')| ≤ c i` match the note's `replacing one observation changes Z by at most 2/m` step, so the plan does NOT rebuild the Doob/Hoeffding chain of the frozen proof. Search trace: grep `mcdiarmid|BoundedDifference` over ../Causalean → Stat/Concentration/TailBounds/McDiarmid.lean and Stat/Concentration/UniformDeviation/BoundedDifference.lean, both thin FoML re-exports; lean_local_search `mcdiarmid` → four FoML theorems. \\(\\varepsilon_N\\) is a closed real expression; the note itself records that its well-typed domain forces \\(n\\ge1\\) and \\(\\min_e N_e\\ge1\\), so F2 carries those as side conditions rather than as `Real.log` junk-value reasoning.",
