    {
      "id": "def:edge-separated-set",
      "obj_id": "P-2",
      "kind": "definition",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "\\(\\mathcal V_{G,s,\\pi}=\\{\\theta\\in\\Theta_{G,s}:F_{\\pi^{-1}(j),\\pi^{-1}(i)}(\\theta)\\ne0\\text{ for every edge }j\\to i\\text{ of }G\\}\\).",
        "tex_anchor": "",
        "frozen": true,
        "frozen_body": "For a target-label permutation \\(\\pi\\), define\n\\[\n\\mathcal V_{G,s,\\pi}\n=\n\\left\\{\n\\theta\\in\\Theta_{G,s}:\nF^{\\mathrm{can}}_{\\pi^{-1}(j),\\pi^{-1}(i)}(\\theta;\\pi)\\ne0\n\\text{ for every edge }j\\to i\\text{ of }G\n\\right\\}.\n\\]\nHere \\(F^{\\mathrm{can}}_{ab}(\\theta;\\pi)\\) is the second-moment contrast in the canonical observed world generated by \\(\\theta\\) and \\(\\pi\\):\n\\[\nF^{\\mathrm{can}}_{ab}(\\theta;\\pi)\n=\n\\int\n\\left(\n\\frac{q_{\\pi(b)}(v_{\\pi(b)})}\n     {p_{\\pi(b)}(v_{\\pi(b)}\\mid v_{\\operatorname{pa}_G(\\pi(b))})}\n\\right)^2\n\\,dP^{\\pi(a)}(v)\n-\n\\int\n\\left(\n\\frac{q_{\\pi(b)}(v_{\\pi(b)})}\n     {p_{\\pi(b)}(v_{\\pi(b)}\\mid v_{\\operatorname{pa}_G(\\pi(b))})}\n\\right)^2\n\\,dP^0(v).\n\\]",
        "frozen_title": "Edge separation set"
      },
      "lean": {
        "decl_name": "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.edgeSeparatedSet",
        "file": "Helpers/Kernel.lean"
      },
      "review": {
        "status": "matched",
        "passed_hash": "5e7c8899a157e8f30dbce7f96448861b16f04824",
        "note": "Membership quantifies over exactly every edge j→i and requires the paper's second-moment contrast at environment labels π⁻¹(j), π⁻¹(i) to be nonzero."
      },
      "proof": {
        "state": "complete",
        "sorry_count": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "def:cover-separated-set",
      "obj_id": "P-3",
      "kind": "definition",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "\\(\\mathcal U_{G,s,\\pi}=\\{\\theta\\in\\Theta_{G,s}:D_{ji}(\\theta)>0\\text{ whenever }\\pi(j)\\lessdot_G\\pi(i)\\}\\).",
        "tex_anchor": "",
        "frozen": true,
        "frozen_body": "Let \\(H\\) be a complete real Hilbert space, and let \\(U\\) be a feature map \\(\\phi:\\mathbb R\\to H\\) satisfying\n\\[\n\\|\\phi(r)\\|_H=1,\n\\qquad\n\\langle \\phi(a),\\phi(b)\\rangle_H=k(a,b)\n\\]\nfor all \\(r,a,b\\in\\mathbb R\\).  For a target permutation \\(\\pi\\), let \\(W_{\\theta,\\pi}^{\\mathrm{can}}\\) be the canonical observed world generated by \\(\\theta\\) and \\(\\pi\\): the mixing and unmixing maps are the identity, the target permutation is \\(\\pi\\), the observational environment has law induced by \\(\\theta\\)'s observational law, intervention environment \\(e\\) has law induced by the intervention targeting \\(\\pi(e)\\), and its ratio carrier is\n\\[\nR_e(v)=\n\\frac{q_{\\pi(e)}(v_{\\pi(e)})}\n{p_{\\pi(e)}(v_{\\pi(e)}\\mid v_{\\operatorname{pa}_G(\\pi(e))})}.\n\\]\nThe cover-separated set is\n\\[\n\\mathcal U_{G,s,\\pi}\n=\n\\left\\{\n\\theta\\in\\Theta_{G,s}:\nD_{ji}\\!\\left(W_{\\theta,\\pi}^{\\mathrm{can}}\\right)>0\n\\ \\text{for every } j,i\\in[n]\\text{ with }\\pi(j)\\lessdot_G\\pi(i)\n\\right\\},\n\\]\nwhere\n\\[\nD_{ji}\\!\\left(W_{\\theta,\\pi}^{\\mathrm{can}}\\right)\n=\n\\left\\|\n\\int \\phi(r)\\,d\\mathsf P^0_{\\theta,\\pi,i}(r)\n-\n\\int \\phi(r)\\,d\\mathsf P^j_{\\theta,\\pi,i}(r)\n\\right\\|_H,\n\\]\n\\(\\mathsf P^0_{\\theta,\\pi,i}\\) is the law of ratio \\(i\\) under the observational environment of \\(W_{\\theta,\\pi}^{\\mathrm{can}}\\), and \\(\\mathsf P^j_{\\theta,\\pi,i}\\) is the law of ratio \\(i\\) under intervention environment \\(j\\) of \\(W_{\\theta,\\pi}^{\\mathrm{can}}\\).",
        "frozen_title": "Cover-separated mechanisms"
      },
      "lean": {
        "decl_name": "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.coverSeparatedSet",
        "file": "Helpers/Kernel.lean",
        "supporting_decls": [
          "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.populationDiscrepancy",
          "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.canonicalObservedWorld"
        ]
      },
      "review": {
        "status": "matched",
        "passed_hash": "e590b839857b3981dabce719da44c7abef02d28a",
        "note": "Renaming the Lean cover indices by π⁻¹ gives exactly D_ji>0 whenever π(j) is ancestrally covered by π(i); every UnitNormFeatureMap realizes the same Gaussian kernel and hence the same MMD."
      },
      "proof": {
        "state": "complete",
        "sorry_count": 0
      }
    },
    {
