        "passed_hash": "6b9bba330043ddc84924702f6ffb039426474c23",
        "note": "After unfolding sparseP, sparseQ, reflectedCoordinate, and threeNodeDAG, Lean gives exactly the reflected 1→2 sparse mechanism with the stated h, normalized exponential q_i, child conditional, and unit remaining p_i."
      },
      "proof": {
        "state": "complete",
        "sorry_count": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "def:affine-path",
      "obj_id": "P-5",
      "kind": "definition",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "For any \\(\\theta=((p_i,q_i))_{i=1}^{n}\\in\\Theta_{G,s}\\) and a chosen edge \\(j\\to i\\), embed the reflected edge-specific version of \\(\\theta^{\\mathrm{sp}}\\) in \\(G\\) and set \\(p_\\ell^t=(1-t)p_\\ell+t p_\\ell^{\\mathrm{sp}}\\) and \\(q_\\ell^t=(1-t)q_\\ell+t q_\\ell^{\\mathrm{sp}}\\) for \\(t\\in[0,1]\\).",
        "tex_anchor": "",
        "frozen": true,
        "frozen_body": "For a finite labeled DAG \\(G\\) on \\([n]\\), a sign vector \\(s\\in\\{-1,1\\}^{[n]}\\), a stratum point \\(\\theta=((p_\\ell,q_\\ell))_{\\ell=1}^n\\in\\Theta_{G,s}\\) as in \\cref{obj:def:model-stratum}, an edge \\(j\\to i\\) in \\(G\\), and \\(t\\in[0,1]\\), define the reflected edge-specific sparse endpoint \\(\\theta^{\\mathrm{sp}}=((p_\\ell^{\\mathrm{sp}},q_\\ell^{\\mathrm{sp}}))_{\\ell=1}^n\\) in \\(G\\) by\n\\[\np_\\ell^{\\mathrm{sp}}(v)=\n\\begin{cases}\n1+\\dfrac{1}{10}\\,h(\\operatorname{reflect}(s_j,v_j))\\,h(\\operatorname{reflect}(s_i,v_i)), & \\ell=i,\\\\\n1, & \\ell\\ne i,\n\\end{cases}\n\\qquad\nq_\\ell^{\\mathrm{sp}}(z)=\n\\dfrac{4\\exp(4\\,\\operatorname{reflect}(s_\\ell,z))}{\\exp(4)-1},\n\\]\nwhere \\(h(x)=2x-1\\). The affine path \\(\\theta^t=((p_\\ell^t,q_\\ell^t))_{\\ell=1}^n\\) is the mechanism on \\(G\\) with\n\\[\np_\\ell^t(v)=(1-t)p_\\ell(v)+t\\,p_\\ell^{\\mathrm{sp}}(v),\n\\qquad\nq_\\ell^t(z)=(1-t)q_\\ell(z)+t\\,q_\\ell^{\\mathrm{sp}}(z),\n\\qquad \\ell\\in[n].\n\\]",
        "frozen_title": "Edge affine path"
      },
      "lean": {
        "decl_name": "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.affinePath",
        "file": "Helpers/Witnesses.lean",
        "supporting_decls": [
          "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.affinePathExtension",
          "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.embeddedSparseWitness"
        ]
      },
      "review": {
        "status": "matched",
        "passed_hash": "06d9e29c8231864744bb865e07d43e0495640590",
        "note": "After unfolding affinePathExtension and embeddedSparseWitness, Lean quantifies over θ∈Θ_{G,s}, an edge j→i, and t∈[0,1], and applies the stated nodewise affine interpolation toward the reflected edge-specific sparse endpoint."
      },
      "proof": {
        "state": "complete",
        "sorry_count": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "def:cancellation-witness",
      "obj_id": "P-6",
      "kind": "definition",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "On \\(1\\to2\\) with node \\(3\\) isolated, set \\(q_i(z)=4\\exp(4z)/(\\exp(4)-1)\\), \\(p_1=p_3=1\\), \\(h(y)=2y-1\\), \\(H(x)=(\\exp(4x)-1)/(\\exp(4)-1)-x\\), and \\(p_2(y\\mid x)=1+0.1H(x)h(y)\\); obtain other sign vectors by coordinate reflections.",
        "tex_anchor": "",
        "frozen": true,
        "frozen_body": "On the graph \\(1\\to2\\) with node \\(3\\) isolated, define \\(\\theta^{\\mathrm{can}}\\) by\n\\[\nq_i(z)=\\frac{4\\exp(4z)}{\\exp(4)-1},\n\\qquad\np_1=1,\n\\qquad\np_3=1,\n\\]\n\\[\nh(y)=2y-1,\n\\qquad\nH(x)=\\frac{\\exp(4x)-1}{\\exp(4)-1}-x,\n\\qquad\np_2(y\\mid x)=1+0.1H(x)h(y).\n\\]\nFor any other sign vector, \\(\\theta^{\\mathrm{can}}\\) is obtained from this mechanism by coordinate reflections.",
