    {
      "id": "def:population-decoder",
      "obj_id": "P-7",
      "kind": "definition",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "From \\((P^0,\\ldots,P^n)\\), compute every \\(R_i\\) and \\(D_{ji}\\), form \\(H_D=\\{j\\to i:D_{ji}>0\\}\\), select a topological ordering of \\(H_D\\), construct every coordinate \\(U_i=C_i(L_i\\mid L_{B_i})\\), and align environment \\(i\\) with \\(U_i\\). For each \\(i\\), range over all subsets \\(A\\subseteq B_i\\), evaluate \\(U_i\\mathbin{\\perp\\!\\!\\!\\perp}_{P^0}U_{B_i\\setminus A}\\mid U_A\\) under the observational law \\(P^0\\), and return the environment-label DAG whose parent set at \\(i\\) is the unique inclusion-minimal subset satisfying this conditional independence.",
        "tex_anchor": "",
        "frozen": true,
        "frozen_body": "Given observed laws \\((P^0,\\ldots,P^n)\\), the population decoder \\(\\mathscr D\\) is defined by the following steps.\n\\begin{enumerate}\n\\item Compute the likelihood ratios and log-ratios\n\\[\nR_i=\\frac{dP^i}{dP^0},\n\\qquad\nL_i=\\log R_i,\n\\qquad i\\in[n],\n\\]\nand the Gaussian-MMD discrepancies \\(D_{ji}\\).\n\n\\item Form the observable directed ratio-discrepancy graph\n\\[\nH_D=\\{j\\to i:D_{ji}>0\\}.\n\\]\n\n\\item Choose a topological ordering of \\(H_D\\). For each \\(i\\), let \\(B_i\\) be the predecessors of \\(i\\) in that ordering and define\n\\[\nU_i=C_i(L_i\\mid L_{B_i}).\n\\]\n\n\\item Align environment \\(i\\) with coordinate \\(U_i\\).\n\n\\item For each \\(i\\), range over \\(A\\subseteq B_i\\) and identify the unique inclusion-minimal subset satisfying\n\\[\nU_i\\mathbin{\\perp\\!\\!\\!\\perp}_{P^0}U_{B_i\\setminus A}\\mid U_A.\n\\]\nThe output is the environment-label DAG\n\\[\nG^\\pi_{\\mathscr D}\n=\n\\{a\\to i:\\ a\\in A_i^{\\min}\\},\n\\qquad\nA_i^{\\min}\n=\n\\min_{\\subseteq}\n\\left\\{\nA\\subseteq B_i:\nU_i\\mathbin{\\perp\\!\\!\\!\\perp}_{P^0}U_{B_i\\setminus A}\\mid U_A\n\\right\\}.\n\\]\n\\end{enumerate}",
        "frozen_title": "Population decoder $\\mathscr D$"
      },
      "lean": {
        "decl_name": "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.populationDecoder",
        "file": "Helpers/Decoder.lean"
      },
      "review": {
        "status": "matched",
        "passed_hash": "fedb249b337343d899de7b4aa1eeae93504d0e97",
        "note": "The Lean tuple computes the law-derived Gaussian-MMD graph, selects a topological order, constructs intervention-specific conditional-rank coordinates, and forms the DAG from unique inclusion-minimal observational conditional-independence sets; its total fallback branches are outside the construction's intrinsic acyclic and unique-minimum domain."
      },
      "proof": {
        "state": "complete",
        "sorry_count": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "def:sample-split-confidence-graph",
      "obj_id": "P-8",
      "kind": "definition",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "Fit \\(\\widehat R_i\\) on training folds, compute \\(\\widehat D_{ji}\\) on independent evaluation folds, and put \\(j\\to i\\) in \\(\\widehat H\\) exactly when \\(\\widehat D_{ji}-\\varepsilon_N(\\alpha,\\eta)>0\\).",
        "tex_anchor": "",
        "frozen": true,
        "frozen_body": "Under \\cref{obj:ass:independent-environment-sampling}, with training and evaluation folds and tuning levels \\(\\alpha,\\eta\\), the sample-split confidence graph \\(\\widehat H\\) is defined by the following steps.\n\\begin{enumerate}\n\\item On the training folds, fit likelihood-ratio estimators\n\\[\n\\widehat R_i,\n\\qquad i\\in[n].\n\\]\n\n\\item On the independent evaluation folds, compute the empirical Gaussian-MMD discrepancies\n\\[\n\\widehat D_{ji},\n\\qquad j,i\\in[n],\\ j\\ne i,\n\\]\nusing \\(\\widehat R_i\\).\n\n\\item Output the directed graph\n\\[\n\\widehat H\n=\n\\left\\{\nj\\to i:\n\\widehat D_{ji}-\\varepsilon_N(\\alpha,\\eta)>0\n\\right\\}.\n\\]\n\\end{enumerate}",
        "frozen_title": "Sample-split confidence graph $\\widehat H$"
      },
      "lean": {
        "decl_name": "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.sampleSplitConfidenceGraph",
        "file": "Helpers/Inference.lean"
      },
      "review": {
        "status": "matched",
        "passed_hash": "292e77a2545cbfd3c4c527ccf3a26faa90a2f58d",
        "note": "Unfolding empiricalDiscrepancy and confidenceRadius shows that an admissible non-self arrow j→i is selected exactly when the training-fitted, evaluation-fold discrepancy satisfies D̂_ji−ε_N(α,η)>0; the sampling premise supplies the stated fold independence."
      },
      "proof": {
        "state": "complete",
        "sorry_count": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "def:bounded-holder-subclass",
      "obj_id": "P-9",
      "kind": "definition",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "\\(\\Theta^{\\beta}_{G,s}(c,M,K,\\rho)=\\{\\theta\\in\\Theta_{G,s}:\\text{ass:bounded-holder-radius, ass:density-lower-envelope, ass:own-derivative-margin, ass:common-interior-domain, ass:bounded-shared-mixing-geometry, ass:observed-log-ratio-regularity, and ass:conditional-design-envelope hold for }n,G,s,\\beta,c,M,K,\\rho\\}\\).",
        "tex_anchor": "",
        "frozen": true,
        "frozen_body": "The bounded Hölder subclass is\n\\[\n\\Theta^{\\beta}_{G,s}(c,M,K,\\rho)\n=\n\\left\\{\n\\theta\\in\\Theta_{G,s}:\n\\begin{array}{l}\n\\text{\\cref{obj:ass:bounded-holder-radius} holds for } n,G,s,\\beta,c,M,K,\\rho,\\\\\n\\text{\\cref{obj:ass:density-lower-envelope} holds for } n,G,s,\\beta,c,M,K,\\rho,\\\\\n\\text{\\cref{obj:ass:own-derivative-margin} holds for } n,G,s,\\beta,c,M,K,\\rho,\\\\\n\\text{\\cref{obj:ass:common-interior-domain} holds for } n,G,s,\\beta,c,M,K,\\rho,\\\\\n\\text{\\cref{obj:ass:bounded-shared-mixing-geometry} holds for } n,G,s,\\beta,c,M,K,\\rho,\\\\\n\\text{\\cref{obj:ass:observed-log-ratio-regularity} holds for } n,G,s,\\beta,c,M,K,\\rho,\\\\\n\\text{\\cref{obj:ass:conditional-design-envelope} holds for } n,G,s,\\beta,c,M,K,\\rho\n\\end{array}\n\\right\\}.\n\\]",
        "frozen_title": "Bounded Hölder subclass $\\Theta^{\\beta}_{G,s}(c,M,K,\\rho)$"
      },
      "lean": {
        "decl_name": "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.BoundedHolderSubclass",
        "file": "Helpers/BoundedSubclass.lean"
      },
      "review": {
        "status": "matched",
        "passed_hash": "e814b6ea253ef8201e03168211babcd0af36dc99",
        "note": "StratumPoint supplies exactly θ ∈ Θ_{G,s}; after unfolding, BoundedHolderSubclass is inhabited iff all seven named conditions hold at the same β, c, M, K, and ρ, while the generated-world and decoder-selected-regime parameters supply the paper’s f, L_i, B_i, and law-derived density background without altering the extension."
      },
      "proof": {
