        "sorry_count": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "def:first-stage-ratio-contract",
      "obj_id": "P-10",
      "kind": "definition",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "\\(\\mathcal E_N^{\\infty}(b_N)=\\{\\max_{i\\in[n]}\\|\\log\\widehat R_i-\\log R_i\\|_{C^1(\\mathcal X)}\\le b_N\\}\\), with the contract \\(\\inf_{\\theta\\in\\Theta^{\\beta}_{G,s}(c,M,K,\\rho)}\\Pr_\\theta\\{\\mathcal E_N^{\\infty}(b_N)\\}\\ge1-\\eta_N\\).",
        "tex_anchor": "",
        "frozen": true,
        "frozen_body": "For a generated observed-world assignment \\(W_\\theta\\), a decoder-selected bounded-regime assignment \\(R_\\theta\\), sample-split experiments \\(S_{\\theta,N}\\), a common environment sample-size sequence \\(N\\mapsto (N_e(N))_{e=0}^n\\), rate sequences \\(b_N\\) and \\(\\eta_N\\), and subclass parameters \\(\\beta,c,M,K,\\rho\\), define\n\\[\n\\mathcal E_N^{\\infty}(b_N)\n=\n\\left\\{\n\\omega:\n\\begin{array}{l}\n\\text{for every } i\\in[n],\\ \n\\log \\widehat R_i(\\omega,\\cdot)\\text{ and }L_i\\text{ are }C^1\\text{ on }\\mathcal X,\\\\\n\\text{and for every }x\\in\\mathcal X,\\ \n\\left|\\log \\widehat R_i(\\omega,x)-L_i(x)\\right|\\le b_N,\\\\\n\\left\\|D_x\\log \\widehat R_i(\\omega,x)-D_xL_i(x)\\right\\|\\le b_N\n\\end{array}\n\\right\\}.\n\\]\nThe first-stage ratio contract holds when the following conditions are satisfied:\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item \\textbf{(Vanishing positive rates.)} For every \\(N\\), \\(b_N>0\\) and \\(\\eta_N>0\\), and both sequences satisfy \\(b_N\\to0\\) and \\(\\eta_N\\to0\\) as \\(N\\to\\infty\\).\n\\item \\textbf{(Common selected-regime schedules.)} For every \\(N\\) and every \\(\\theta\\in\\Theta^{\\beta}_{G,s}(c,M,K,\\rho)\\) as in \\cref{obj:def:bounded-holder-subclass}, the selected bounded regime \\(R_\\theta\\) has environment sample-size sequence \\(N\\mapsto (N_e(N))_{e=0}^n\\), ratio-error rate \\(b_N\\), and first-stage failure rate \\(\\eta_N\\).\n\\item \\textbf{(Sampling design.)} For every \\(N\\) and every \\(\\theta\\in\\Theta^{\\beta}_{G,s}(c,M,K,\\rho)\\), the experiment \\(S_{\\theta,N}\\) satisfies the independent-environment sample-splitting conditions in \\cref{obj:ass:independent-environment-sampling}, and its environment sample sizes are exactly \\((N_e(N))_{e=0}^n\\).\n\\item \\textbf{(Measurable high-probability event.)} For every \\(N\\) and every \\(\\theta\\in\\Theta^{\\beta}_{G,s}(c,M,K,\\rho)\\), the event \\(\\mathcal E_N^{\\infty}(b_N)\\) is measurable under \\(S_{\\theta,N}\\), and\n\\[\n1-\\eta_N\n\\le\n\\Pr_{S_{\\theta,N}}\\left\\{\\mathcal E_N^{\\infty}(b_N)\\right\\}.\n\\]\n\\end{itemize}",
        "frozen_title": "First-stage ratio contract"
      },
      "lean": {
        "decl_name": "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.firstStageRatioContract",
        "file": "Helpers/BoundedSubclass.lean",
        "supporting_decls": [
          "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.uniformC1RatioEvent"
        ]
      },
