    {
      "id": "prop:sparse-witness-certificate",
      "obj_id": "T-1",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "The constructions \\(\\theta^{\\mathrm{sp}}\\) and \\(\\theta^{\\mathrm{can}}\\) are positive, normalized, \\(C^\\infty\\), faithful to \\(1\\to2\\) plus isolated node \\(3\\), and satisfy the prescribed derivative signs after reflection. The sparse witness obeys \\(\\mathbb E_{P^0}[R_2^2]-\\mathbb E_{P^1}[R_2^2]>3\\times10^{-4}\\) and \\(D_{12}>5\\times10^{-8}\\), whereas the entire direct-edge ratio law under \\(\\theta^{\\mathrm{can}}\\) is identical in environments \\(0\\) and \\(1\\), so \\(D_{12}=0\\).",
        "tex_anchor": "",
        "frozen": true,
        "frozen_body": "For every sign vector \\(s\\in\\{-1,1\\}^3\\), let \\(\\theta^{\\mathrm{sp}}\\) be the construction in \\cref{obj:def:sparse-witness} and let \\(\\theta^{\\mathrm{can}}\\) be the construction in \\cref{obj:def:cancellation-witness}, both on the three-node DAG \\(1\\to2\\) with node \\(3\\) isolated. Let \\(W^{\\mathrm{sp}}\\) and \\(W^{\\mathrm{can}}\\) be the corresponding observed worlds with identity mixing and identity target permutation, so that environment \\(0\\) has the observational law, environment \\(e\\) has the intervention law at target \\(e\\), and\n\\[\nR_i(v)=\\frac{q_i(v_i)}{p_i(v_i\\mid v_{\\operatorname{pa}_G(i)})}.\n\\]\nThen:\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item \\textbf{(Sparse witness regularity.)} The mechanism \\(\\theta^{\\mathrm{sp}}\\) satisfies \\cref{obj:ass:positive-normalized-smooth-mechanisms}, \\cref{obj:ass:fixed-own-derivative-sign} with sign vector \\(s\\), and \\cref{obj:ass:faithfulness}. Moreover, every observational conditional density \\(p_i^{\\mathrm{sp}}\\) is \\(C^\\infty\\) on \\([0,1]^3\\), and every intervention density \\(q_i^{\\mathrm{sp}}\\) is \\(C^\\infty\\) on \\([0,1]\\).\n\\item \\textbf{(Cancellation witness regularity.)} The mechanism \\(\\theta^{\\mathrm{can}}\\) satisfies \\cref{obj:ass:positive-normalized-smooth-mechanisms}, \\cref{obj:ass:fixed-own-derivative-sign} with sign vector \\(s\\), and \\cref{obj:ass:faithfulness}. Moreover, every observational conditional density \\(p_i^{\\mathrm{can}}\\) is \\(C^\\infty\\) on \\([0,1]^3\\), and every intervention density \\(q_i^{\\mathrm{can}}\\) is \\(C^\\infty\\) on \\([0,1]\\).\n\\item \\textbf{(Sparse witness separation.)} The sparse witness has\n\\[\n\\frac{3}{10000}\n<\n\\int R_2(x)^2\\,dP^0_{\\mathrm{sp}}(x)\n-\n\\int R_2(x)^2\\,dP^1_{\\mathrm{sp}}(x),\n\\]\nand its Gaussian-kernel population discrepancy satisfies\n\\[\n\\frac{5}{100000000}<D_{12}(W^{\\mathrm{sp}}).\n\\]\n\\item \\textbf{(Cancellation witness equality.)} For the cancellation witness, the law of \\(R_2\\) under the observational environment equals the law of \\(R_2\\) under environment \\(1\\), and\n\\[\nD_{12}(W^{\\mathrm{can}})=0.\n\\]\n\\end{itemize}",
        "frozen_title": "Sparse witness certificate"
      },
      "lean": {
        "decl_name": "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.sparse_witness_certificate",
        "file": "TSparseWitnessCertificate.lean"
      },
      "review": {
        "status": "matched",
        "passed_hash": "a0fa32c41927a34662459d58fb4d88d5e9ac11ae",
        "note": "After unfolding the witness mechanisms, canonical laws, ratio-law pushforwards, Gaussian feature map, MMD, regularity, sign, and faithfulness predicates, Lean states every paper clause with the same graph, environments, ratio coordinate, strict constants, and equality of the full cancellation ratio laws."
