    {
      "id": "lem:analytic-edge-perturbation",
      "obj_id": "L-1",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "After the harmless target relabeling \\(\\pi=\\operatorname{id}\\), fix \\(\\theta\\in\\Theta_{G,s}\\) and an edge \\(j\\to i\\) of \\(G\\). Along the path \\(\\theta^t\\), \\[F_{ji}(\\theta^t)=\\int_{[0,1]^n}\\frac{(q_i^t)^2(q_j^t-p_j^t)\\prod_{\\ell\\ne i,j}p_\\ell^t}{p_i^t}\\,dv\\] is real analytic on an open interval containing \\([0,1]\\), is nonzero at \\(t=1\\), and has isolated zeros. For every relative \\(C^2\\) neighborhood of \\(\\theta\\), some sufficiently small \\(t>0\\) remains in \\(\\Theta_{G,s}\\) and satisfies \\(F_{ji}(\\theta^t)\\ne0\\).",
        "tex_anchor": "",
        "frozen": true,
        "frozen_body": "After the harmless target relabeling \\(\\pi=\\operatorname{id}\\), fix the ambient number \\(n\\) of scalar latent variables, a finite labeled DAG \\(G\\) on \\([n]\\), a sign vector \\(s\\in\\{-1,1\\}^{[n]}\\), a mechanism \\(\\theta\\in\\Theta_{G,s}\\) as in \\cref{obj:def:model-stratum}, and an edge \\(j\\to i\\) of \\(G\\). Assume that the identity-target canonical observed world generated by \\(\\theta\\) satisfies \\cref{obj:ass:one-perfect-intervention-per-node}. Let \\(\\theta^t\\) be the edge-specific affine path of \\cref{obj:def:affine-path}, and write \\(F_{ji}(\\eta)\\) for the direct-edge second-moment contrast computed in the identity-target canonical observed world generated by a mechanism \\(\\eta\\). Along this path,\n\\[\nF_{ji}(\\theta^t)\n=\n\\int_{[0,1]^n}\n\\frac{(q_i^t(v_i))^2\\bigl(q_j^t(v_j)-p_j^t(v_j\\mid v_{\\operatorname{pa}_G(j)})\\bigr)\n\\prod_{\\ell\\ne i,j}p_\\ell^t(v_\\ell\\mid v_{\\operatorname{pa}_G(\\ell)})}\n{p_i^t(v_i\\mid v_{\\operatorname{pa}_G(i)})}\n\\,dv .\n\\]\nThere is an open set \\(O\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\) with \\([0,1]\\subseteq O\\) such that:\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item \\textbf{(Integral identity.)} For every \\(t\\in O\\), the displayed integral equals \\(F_{ji}(\\theta^t)\\).\n\\item \\textbf{(Analyticity.)} The map \\(t\\mapsto F_{ji}(\\theta^t)\\) is real analytic on a neighborhood of every point of \\(O\\).\n\\item \\textbf{(Isolated zeros.)} If \\(t\\in O\\) and \\(F_{ji}(\\theta^t)=0\\), then there is \\(\\varepsilon>0\\) such that every \\(u\\in(t-\\varepsilon,t+\\varepsilon)\\) with \\(u\\ne t\\) satisfies \\(F_{ji}(\\theta^u)\\ne0\\).\n\\end{itemize}\nMoreover, \\(F_{ji}(\\theta^1)\\ne0\\). Finally, for every relative \\(C^2\\) neighborhood \\(N\\) of \\(\\theta\\), there exists \\(t\\in(0,1)\\) such that \\(\\theta^t\\in N\\), \\(\\theta^t\\in\\Theta_{G,s}\\), and \\(F_{ji}(\\theta^t)\\ne0\\).",
        "frozen_title": "Analytic edge perturbation"
      },
      "lean": {
        "decl_name": "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.analytic_edge_perturbation",
        "file": "Helpers/AnalyticEdgePerturbation.lean"
      },
      "review": {
        "status": "matched",
        "passed_hash": "c98b788196f15a18293796bf716101fe71cd138c",
        "note": "The unfolded contrast, affine path, stratum preservation, endpoint nonvanishing, isolated-zero condition, and arbitrarily close relative-C² perturbation are equivalent; the canonical intervention premise follows from the stratum's positive normalized mechanisms, and the open set can be restricted to an open interval containing [0,1]."
      },
      "proof": {
        "state": "complete",
        "sorry_count": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "thm:generic-cover-separation",
      "obj_id": "T-2",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "For every finite labeled DAG \\(G\\), sign vector \\(s\\), and target permutation \\(\\pi\\) with \\(\\Theta_{G,s}\\ne\\varnothing\\), the set \\(\\mathcal V_{G,s,\\pi}\\) is open dense in \\(\\Theta_{G,s}\\). Therefore \\(\\mathcal U_{G,s,\\pi}\\) is open dense and residual, and its complement is closed nowhere dense. For the empty graph, both sets equal \\(\\Theta_{G,s}\\).",
        "tex_anchor": "",
        "frozen": true,
        "frozen_body": "Let \\(n\\) be the ambient number of scalar latent variables. Assume:\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item \\textbf{(Finite labeled DAG.)} \\(G\\) is a finite labeled DAG on \\([n]\\).\n\\item \\textbf{(Sign stratum.)} \\(s\\) is a sign vector with coordinates in \\(\\{-1,1\\}\\), and the stratum \\(\\Theta_{G,s}\\) of \\cref{obj:def:model-stratum} is nonempty.\n\\item \\textbf{(Target permutation.)} \\(\\pi\\) is a permutation of \\([n]\\).\n\\end{itemize}\nLet \\(\\mathcal V_{G,s,\\pi}\\) be the direct-edge separation set of \\cref{obj:def:edge-separated-set}, and let \\(\\mathcal U_{G,s,\\pi}\\) be the ancestral-cover separation set of \\cref{obj:def:cover-separated-set} formed with the Gaussian feature map \\(\\phi(a)=k(a,\\cdot)\\) for \\(k(a,b)=\\exp\\{-(a-b)^2\\}\\). Then \\(\\mathcal V_{G,s,\\pi}\\) is open and dense in \\(\\Theta_{G,s}\\), and\n\\[\n\\mathcal V_{G,s,\\pi}\\subseteq \\mathcal U_{G,s,\\pi}.\n\\]\nMoreover, \\(\\mathcal U_{G,s,\\pi}\\) is open and dense in \\(\\Theta_{G,s}\\), and its complement in \\(\\Theta_{G,s}\\) is meagre, closed, and nowhere dense. If \\(G\\) has no directed edges, then\n\\[\n\\mathcal V_{G,s,\\pi}=\\Theta_{G,s}\n\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n\\mathcal U_{G,s,\\pi}=\\Theta_{G,s}.\n\\]",
        "frozen_title": "Generic cover separation"
      },
      "lean": {
        "decl_name": "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.generic_cover_separation",
        "file": "TGenericCoverSeparation.lean"
      },
      "review": {
        "status": "matched",
        "passed_hash": "86492e03fea23fdc2a0ac783a1ea148535293799",
        "note": "The nonemptiness premise is equivalent to Θ_{G,s} ≠ ∅; openness, density, residuality via meagre complement, closed nowhere-dense complement, and the edge-free equalities match exactly, while the extra V ⊆ U conjunct follows unconditionally from the unfolded separation definitions."
      },
      "proof": {
        "state": "complete",
        "sorry_count": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "thm:exact-ratio-decoder",
      "obj_id": "T-3",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "For every mechanism in \\(\\mathcal U_{G,s,\\pi}\\), the observed laws \\((P^0,\\ldots,P^n)\\) identify the latent representation and structure via \\(\\mathscr D\\): \\(\\operatorname{TC}(H_D)=\\operatorname{TC}(G^\\pi)\\); each \\(U_i\\) equals \\(Q_{\\pi(i)}(V_{\\pi(i)})\\) when \\(s_{\\pi(i)}=+1\\) and \\(1-Q_{\\pi(i)}(V_{\\pi(i)})\\) when \\(s_{\\pi(i)}=-1\\); and environment \\(i\\) is thereby aligned with its recovered coordinate. Every topological ordering of \\(H_D\\) places the environment-label parent set \\(\\pi^{-1}(\\operatorname{pa}_G(\\pi(i)))\\) inside \\(B_i\\). Under the observational law \\(P^0\\), for every \\(i\\in[n]\\) and every subset \\(A\\subseteq B_i\\), \\[U_i\\mathbin{\\perp\\!\\!\\!\\perp}_{P^0}U_{B_i\\setminus A}\\mid U_A\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad \\pi^{-1}(\\operatorname{pa}_G(\\pi(i)))\\subseteq A.\\] Consequently causal minimality makes \\(\\pi^{-1}(\\operatorname{pa}_G(\\pi(i)))\\) the unique inclusion-minimal admissible conditioning set, so parent pruning returns exactly \\(G^\\pi\\), independently of the selected topological ordering. Any compatible causal-minimal representation satisfying the same positive normalized scalar perfect-intervention, shared \\(C^2\\)-mixing, and own-derivative conditions differs only by simultaneous relabeling and componentwise \\(C^2\\) diffeomorphisms. On the overlapping positive \\(C^3\\) compact-cube, \\(C^2\\)-mixing faithful regime, this improves the arbitrary-dimensional intervention count of von Kugelgen et al. (2023, Theorem 3.4) from two perfect interventions per node to one. Within the present regime, the decoding and uniqueness conclusions extend structurally from faithful to causal-minimal mechanisms; they do not settle the anchor's full \\(\\mathbb R^n\\), \\(C^1\\) class. At \\(n=2\\), Gaussian-MMD positivity supplies the continuous law-separation witness used in their Theorem 3.2. Relative to Wendong et al. (2023, Theorem 4.2) and Yao et al. (2025, Corollary D.1), the decoder recovers rather than takes as given the graph or topological order and intervention alignment.",
        "tex_anchor": "",
        "frozen": true,
        "frozen_body": "Fix \\(n\\), a finite labelled DAG \\(G\\) on \\([n]\\), and a sign vector \\(s\\in\\{-1,+1\\}^{[n]}\\). Let \\(\\theta=(p_i,q_i)_{i\\in[n]}\\) be a mechanism on \\(G\\). Let \\(\\mathsf{world}\\) assign an observed world to every mechanism on \\(G\\), and write \\(W=\\mathsf{world}(\\theta)\\), with shared mixing map \\(f\\), inverse map \\(f^{-1}\\), target permutation \\(\\pi\\), observed laws \\((P^0,\\ldots,P^n)\\), likelihood ratios \\(R_i=dP^i/dP^0\\), and log-ratios \\(L_i=\\log R_i\\). Assume:\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item \\textbf{(Smooth positive mechanisms.)} \\(\\theta\\) satisfies \\cref{obj:ass:positive-normalized-smooth-mechanisms}.\n\\item \\textbf{(Causal minimality.)} \\(\\theta\\) satisfies \\cref{obj:ass:causal-minimality}.\n\\item \\textbf{(Shared mixing.)} The maps \\(f\\) and \\(f^{-1}\\) in \\(W\\) satisfy \\cref{obj:ass:shared-diffeomorphic-mixing}.\n\\item \\textbf{(One intervention per node.)} The laws \\((P^0,\\ldots,P^n)\\), ratios \\((R_i)_{i\\in[n]}\\), and target permutation \\(\\pi\\) in \\(W\\) satisfy \\cref{obj:ass:one-perfect-intervention-per-node}.\n\\item \\textbf{(Own-derivative signs.)} \\(\\theta\\) satisfies \\cref{obj:ass:fixed-own-derivative-sign} with sign vector \\(s\\).\n\\item \\textbf{(Gaussian cover separation.)} The stratum point \\(\\theta\\in\\Theta_{G,s}\\) belongs to the cover-separated set of \\cref{obj:def:cover-separated-set} with the Gaussian unit-norm feature map associated with \\(k(a,b)=\\exp\\{-(a-b)^2\\}\\) and target permutation \\(\\pi\\); equivalently, every transported ancestral cover has strictly positive population Gaussian-MMD discrepancy.\n\\end{itemize}\nLet \\(\\mathscr D\\) be the population decoder of \\cref{obj:def:population-decoder}, let \\(H_D=\\{j\\to i:D_{ji}>0\\}\\), and let \\(G^\\pi\\) be the environment-label DAG. Then\n\\[\n\\operatorname{TC}(H_D)=\\operatorname{TC}(G^\\pi).\n\\]\nThe ordering selected by \\(\\mathscr D\\) is a topological ordering of \\(H_D\\). For every topological ordering of \\(H_D\\), with predecessor set \\(B_i\\) for node \\(i\\), and every \\(i\\in[n]\\), the selected conditional CDF \\(C_i(t\\mid L_{B_i})\\) is a continuous version of the conditional ratio CDF. For each such \\(i\\), there exists a continuous version \\(C\\) such that, for every latent point \\(v\\) in the latent cube,\n\\[\nC\\!\\left(t\\,\\middle|\\,L_{B_i}(f(v))\\right)\n=\nC_{\\theta,\\pi(i)}^{\\mathrm{str}}(t\\mid v).\n\\]\nEvery continuous version agrees with the selected \\(C_i\\) on the observed conditional-ratio support, and the selected version satisfies the same structural identity at every mixed latent point \\(f(v)\\). Consequently, for every \\(v\\) in the latent cube,\n\\[\nU_i(f(v))=\n\\begin{cases}\nQ_{\\pi(i)}(v_{\\pi(i)}), & s_{\\pi(i)}=1,\\\\\n1-Q_{\\pi(i)}(v_{\\pi(i)}), & s_{\\pi(i)}=-1.\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\nFor every topological ordering of \\(H_D\\) and every \\(i\\in[n]\\),\n\\[\n\\pi^{-1}\\!\\bigl(\\operatorname{pa}_G(\\pi(i))\\bigr)\\subseteq B_i.\n\\]\nUnder \\(P^0\\), for every such ordering, every \\(i\\in[n]\\), and every \\(A\\subseteq B_i\\),\n\\[\nU_i\\perp\\!\\!\\!\\perp U_{B_i\\setminus A}\\mid U_A\n\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n\\pi^{-1}\\!\\bigl(\\operatorname{pa}_G(\\pi(i))\\bigr)\\subseteq A.\n\\]\nThus, for every such ordering and every \\(i\\), the set\n\\[\n\\pi^{-1}\\!\\bigl(\\operatorname{pa}_G(\\pi(i))\\bigr)\n\\]\nis admissible and is the unique inclusion-minimal admissible parent set. The observed laws are coherent with \\(W\\), and the parent-pruned graph returned by \\(\\mathscr D\\) is exactly \\(G^\\pi\\).\n\nFor any DAG \\(G'\\) on \\([n]\\), mechanism \\(\\theta'\\), and observed world \\(W'\\) satisfying \\cref{obj:ass:positive-normalized-smooth-mechanisms}, \\cref{obj:ass:causal-minimality}, \\cref{obj:ass:fixed-own-derivative-sign} with the same sign vector \\(s\\), \\cref{obj:ass:shared-diffeomorphic-mixing}, and \\cref{obj:ass:one-perfect-intervention-per-node}, equality between the observed environment-law family of \\(W'\\) and the observed environment-law family of \\(W\\) implies that \\(W'\\) is componentwise \\(C^2\\)-equivalent to \\(W\\) up to the simultaneous relabeling encoded by the target permutations. When \\(n=2\\), every edge \\(j\\to i\\) of \\(G\\) has strictly positive observed Gaussian-MMD discrepancy,\n\\[\n0<D_{\\pi^{-1}(j),\\pi^{-1}(i)}.\n\\]\nWithin the positive \\(C^3\\) compact-cube, shared \\(C^2\\)-mixing, causal-minimal regime, \\(\\mathscr D\\) identifies the latent representation and structure from one perfect intervention per node, supplies the continuous law-separation witness used by \\citet[Theorem~3.2]{vonKugelgen2023} when \\(n=2\\), and recovers the graph, topological order, and intervention alignment relative to \\citet[Theorem~4.2]{Wendong2023} and \\citet[Corollary~{D}.1]{Yao2025}.",
        "frozen_title": "Exact ratio decoding"
      },
      "lean": {
        "decl_name": "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.exact_ratio_decoder",
        "file": "TExactRatioDecoder.lean"
      },
      "review": {
        "status": "matched",
        "passed_hash": "3fcf26911f9bc66187b61ca45a7b49863095be1f",
        "note": "After unfolding all referenced definitions, the Lean statement matches the frozen theorem’s mechanism class, transitive-closure and rank recovery, intervention alignment, all-order parent containment and conditional-independence characterization, unique minimal pruning, compatible-representation uniqueness, and comparison/scope clauses; the world-family packaging is conservative because unused fibers impose no restrictions."
      },
      "proof": {
        "state": "complete",
        "sorry_count": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lem:equation-ten-intervention-marginal",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "Let \\(\\tau\\) be a topological ordering of the ratio graph \\(H_D\\) of \\cref{obj:def:population-decoder} that also orders the transported latent DAG, i.e. \\(\\tau(j)<\\tau(i)\\) whenever \\(\\pi(j)\\to\\pi(i)\\) is an edge of \\(G\\); write \\(B_i^\\tau=\\{j:\\tau(j)<\\tau(i)\\}\\) and \\(A_i^\\tau=\\{\\pi(i)\\}\\cup\\pi(B_i^\\tau)\\), and, for \\(v\\in[0,1]^n\\) and \\(r\\in[0,1]^{[n]\\setminus A_i^\\tau}\\), let \\(u^{v,\\tau}(r)\\) be the latent point with \\(u^{v,\\tau}(r)_a=v_a\\) for \\(a\\in A_i^\\tau\\) and \\(u^{v,\\tau}(r)_a=r_a\\) otherwise.  Under \\cref{obj:ass:positive-normalized-smooth-mechanisms}, for every \\(i\\in[n]\\) and every \\(v\\in[0,1]^n\\), eliminating the coordinates outside \\(A_i^\\tau\\) from the target-\\(\\pi(i)\\) latent density leaves the replacement density at the target times the observational factors of the retained non-target coordinates:\n\\[\n\\int_{[0,1]^{[n]\\setminus A_i^\\tau}}\nq_{\\pi(i)}\\!\\left(u^{v,\\tau}(r)_{\\pi(i)}\\right)\n\\prod_{\\ell\\ne\\pi(i)}\np_\\ell\\!\\left(u^{v,\\tau}(r)_\\ell\\mid u^{v,\\tau}(r)_{\\operatorname{pa}_G(\\ell)}\\right)dr\n=\nq_{\\pi(i)}(v_{\\pi(i)})\n\\prod_{\\ell\\in A_i^\\tau\\setminus\\{\\pi(i)\\}}\np_\\ell\\!\\left(v_\\ell\\mid v_{\\operatorname{pa}_G(\\ell)}\\right),\n\\]\nthe integral being taken against Lebesgue measure on the eliminated unit-interval coordinates.",
        "tex_anchor": "",
        "frozen": true,
        "frozen_body": "Fix \\(i\\in[n]\\). Suppose that:\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item \\textbf{(Regular mechanisms.)} The mechanism satisfies \\cref{obj:ass:positive-normalized-smooth-mechanisms}.\n\\item \\textbf{(Ratio-graph order.)} The map \\(\\tau:[n]\\to\\mathbb N\\) is injective and is a topological ordering of the observable ratio-discrepancy graph \\(H_D\\) in \\cref{obj:def:population-decoder}: whenever \\(D_{ji}>0\\), \\(\\tau(j)<\\tau(i)\\).\n\\item \\textbf{(Transported-DAG order.)} The same order respects the transported latent DAG: whenever \\(\\pi(j)\\to\\pi(i)\\) is an edge of \\(G\\), \\(\\tau(j)<\\tau(i)\\).\n\\end{itemize}\nLet\n\\[\nB_i^\\tau=\\{j\\in[n]:\\tau(j)<\\tau(i)\\},\n\\qquad\nA_i^\\tau=\\{\\pi(i)\\}\\cup\\pi(B_i^\\tau).\n\\]\nFor \\(v\\in[0,1]^n\\) and \\(r\\in[0,1]^{[n]\\setminus A_i^\\tau}\\), let \\(u^{v,\\tau}(r)\\in[0,1]^n\\) be the point with\n\\[\nu^{v,\\tau}(r)_a=v_a \\quad(a\\in A_i^\\tau),\n\\qquad\nu^{v,\\tau}(r)_a=r_a \\quad(a\\notin A_i^\\tau).\n\\]\nThen, for every \\(v\\in[0,1]^n\\),\n\\[\n\\int_{[0,1]^{[n]\\setminus A_i^\\tau}}\nq_{\\pi(i)}\\!\\left(u^{v,\\tau}(r)_{\\pi(i)}\\right)\n\\prod_{\\ell\\ne \\pi(i)}\np_\\ell\\!\\left(u^{v,\\tau}(r)_\\ell\\mid\nu^{v,\\tau}(r)_{\\operatorname{pa}_G(\\ell)}\\right)\\,dr\n=\nq_{\\pi(i)}(v_{\\pi(i)})\n\\prod_{\\ell\\in A_i^\\tau\\setminus\\{\\pi(i)\\}}\np_\\ell\\!\\left(v_\\ell\\mid v_{\\operatorname{pa}_G(\\ell)}\\right).\n\\]",
        "frozen_title": "Intervention marginal identity"
      },
      "lean": {
        "decl_name": "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.equationTen_interventionMarginalDensity",
        "file": "Helpers/DecoderConditionalKernel.lean"
      },
      "review": {
        "status": "matched",
        "passed_hash": "1332b8f4e48555d450001524bc70a3ea149914bf",
