      "id": "lem:equation-ten-fiber-product",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "In the setting of \\cref{obj:ass:positive-normalized-smooth-mechanisms}, let \\(\\tau\\) be a topological ordering of the ratio graph \\(H_D\\) of \\cref{obj:def:population-decoder} that also orders the transported latent DAG, i.e. \\(\\tau(j)<\\tau(i)\\) whenever \\(\\pi(j)\\to\\pi(i)\\) is an edge of \\(G\\), and keep the notation \\(B_i^\\tau=\\{j:\\tau(j)<\\tau(i)\\}\\), \\(A_i^\\tau=\\{\\pi(i)\\}\\cup\\pi(B_i^\\tau)\\), and \\(u^{v,\\tau}(r)\\) for the latent point that keeps the coordinates in \\(A_i^\\tau\\) fixed at \\(v\\) and fills the remaining coordinates from \\(r\\).  For \\(v\\in[0,1]^n\\) and \\(w\\in\\mathbb R\\) write \\(v^{(w)}\\) for \\(v\\) with its \\(\\pi(i)\\)-coordinate replaced by \\(w\\).  Then, for every \\(i\\in[n]\\), every \\(v\\in[0,1]^n\\), and every \\(w\\), the eliminated target-\\(\\pi(i)\\) density evaluated at \\(v^{(w)}\\) is the replacement density at \\(w\\) times a factor that does not depend on \\(w\\):\n\\[\n\\int_{[0,1]^{[n]\\setminus A_i^\\tau}}\nq_{\\pi(i)}\\!\\left(u^{v^{(w)},\\tau}(r)_{\\pi(i)}\\right)\n\\prod_{\\ell\\ne\\pi(i)}\np_\\ell\\!\\left(u^{v^{(w)},\\tau}(r)_\\ell\\mid u^{v^{(w)},\\tau}(r)_{\\operatorname{pa}_G(\\ell)}\\right)dr\n=\nq_{\\pi(i)}(w)\n\\prod_{\\ell\\in A_i^\\tau\\setminus\\{\\pi(i)\\}}\np_\\ell\\!\\left(v_\\ell\\mid v_{\\operatorname{pa}_G(\\ell)}\\right),\n\\]\nthe retained non-target factors being evaluated at \\(v\\) itself, so that the predecessor part of the density is constant along the \\(\\pi(i)\\)-fiber.",
        "tex_anchor": "",
        "frozen": true,
        "frozen_body": "In the setting of \\cref{obj:ass:positive-normalized-smooth-mechanisms}, fix an observed world with target permutation \\(\\pi\\).  Let \\(\\tau\\) be a numerical order on \\([n]\\), and fix \\(i\\in[n]\\).  Assume:\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item \\textbf{(Ratio-graph order.)} The order \\(\\tau\\) is injective and topological for the observable ratio graph \\(H_D=\\{j\\to i:j\\ne i,\\ D_{ji}>0\\}\\) of \\cref{obj:def:population-decoder}: whenever \\(D_{ji}>0\\), one has \\(\\tau(j)<\\tau(i)\\).\n\\item \\textbf{(Transported-DAG order.)} The same order respects every transported latent edge: whenever \\(\\pi(j)\\to\\pi(i)\\) is an edge of \\(G\\), one has \\(\\tau(j)<\\tau(i)\\).\n\\end{itemize}\nWrite\n\\[\nB_i^\\tau=\\{j:\\tau(j)<\\tau(i)\\},\n\\qquad\nA_i^\\tau=\\{\\pi(i)\\}\\cup \\pi(B_i^\\tau).\n\\]\nFor \\(x\\in\\mathbb R^n\\) and \\(r\\in[0,1]^{[n]\\setminus A_i^\\tau}\\), let \\(u^{x,\\tau}(r)\\) be the latent point whose coordinates in \\(A_i^\\tau\\) agree with \\(x\\) and whose remaining coordinates are filled by \\(r\\).  For every \\(v\\in\\mathbb R^n\\) and every \\(w\\in\\mathbb R\\), if \\(v^{(w)}\\) denotes \\(v\\) with its \\(\\pi(i)\\)-coordinate replaced by \\(w\\), then\n\\[\n\\int_{[0,1]^{[n]\\setminus A_i^\\tau}}\nq_{\\pi(i)}\\!\\left(u^{v^{(w)},\\tau}(r)_{\\pi(i)}\\right)\n\\prod_{\\ell\\ne\\pi(i)}\np_\\ell\\!\\left(u^{v^{(w)},\\tau}(r)_\\ell\\mid\nu^{v^{(w)},\\tau}(r)_{\\operatorname{pa}_G(\\ell)}\\right)\\,dr\n=\nq_{\\pi(i)}(w)\n\\prod_{\\ell\\in A_i^\\tau\\setminus\\{\\pi(i)\\}}\np_\\ell\\!\\left(v_\\ell\\mid v_{\\operatorname{pa}_G(\\ell)}\\right).\n\\]",
        "frozen_title": "Fiber product factorization"
      },
      "lean": {
        "decl_name": "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.equationTen_interventionMarginalDensity_fiber_product",
        "file": "Helpers/DecoderConditionalKernel.lean"
      },
      "review": {
        "status": "matched",
        "passed_hash": "da19d07b4faba139ced635ef03ff3eea5f10179d",
        "note": "Lean's `equationTen_interventionMarginalDensity_fiber_product` evaluates the same eliminated intervention density at `Function.update v (W.targetPerm i) w`, which is the point v^{(w)} displayed here, and returns `q.density w` times the partial density of the retained non-target coordinates at the unmodified v; the w-independence of that factor is what Lean's `equationTen_predecessorDensity_update_target` supplies inside the proof."
      },
      "proof": {
        "state": "complete",
        "sorry_count": 0
      }
