    {
      "id": "lem:equation-eleven-kernel-factorization",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "Assume \\cref{obj:ass:positive-normalized-smooth-mechanisms,obj:ass:shared-diffeomorphic-mixing,obj:ass:one-perfect-intervention-per-node,obj:ass:fixed-own-derivative-sign} with sign vector \\(s\\), and let \\(\\tau\\) be a topological ordering of the ratio graph \\(H_D\\) of \\cref{obj:def:population-decoder} that also orders the transported latent DAG, i.e. \\(\\tau(j)<\\tau(i)\\) whenever \\(\\pi(j)\\to\\pi(i)\\) is an edge of \\(G\\).  Fix \\(i\\in[n]\\), put \\(B_i^\\tau=\\{j:\\tau(j)<\\tau(i)\\}\\), and let \\(\\kappa_i^\\tau\\) be the Markov kernel from the predecessor log-ratio space \\(\\mathbb R^{B_i^\\tau}\\) to \\(\\mathbb R\\) that assigns to a predecessor log-ratio vector \\(\\ell\\) the law of\n\\[\n\\log\\frac{q_{\\pi(i)}(W)}{p_{\\pi(i)}\\!\\left(\\widetilde v_i^\\tau(z_i^\\tau(\\ell),W)\\right)},\n\\qquad W\\sim q_{\\pi(i)}(w)\\,dw \\text{ on }[0,1],\n\\]\nwhere \\(z_i^\\tau=(\\Lambda_i^\\tau)^{-1}\\circ\\rho_i^\\tau\\) is the triangular predecessor-score inverse composed with the retraction onto the realized score range \\(\\mathcal R_i^\\tau\\), and \\(\\widetilde v_i^\\tau(z,w)\\) is the latent point whose \\(\\pi(j)\\)-coordinate is \\(z_j\\) for \\(j\\in B_i^\\tau\\), whose \\(\\pi(i)\\)-coordinate is \\(w\\), and whose other coordinates are zero.  Then, under the target-\\(\\pi(i)\\) environment law \\(P^i\\), the joint law of the predecessor log-ratios and the target log-ratio factorizes as the composition product of the predecessor marginal with \\(\\kappa_i^\\tau\\):\n\\[\n\\left(L_{B_i^\\tau},L_i\\right)_{\\#}P^i\n=\n\\left(L_{B_i^\\tau}\\right)_{\\#}P^i\\otimes\\kappa_i^\\tau .\n\\]",
        "tex_anchor": "",
        "frozen": true,
        "frozen_body": "Let \\(n\\) be fixed, let \\(G\\) be a finite labeled DAG on \\([n]\\), let \\(s\\) be a sign vector with entries in \\(\\{-1,1\\}\\), and let \\(W\\) be an observed world generated by a mechanism \\(\\theta\\). Assume:\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item \\textbf{(Structural regularity.)} The mechanism and observed world satisfy \\cref{obj:ass:positive-normalized-smooth-mechanisms,obj:ass:shared-diffeomorphic-mixing,obj:ass:one-perfect-intervention-per-node,obj:ass:fixed-own-derivative-sign} with sign vector \\(s\\).\n\\item \\textbf{(Observed ratio order.)} The map \\(\\tau:[n]\\to\\mathbb N\\) is injective and is a topological ordering of the observed Gaussian-MMD ratio graph \\(H_D\\) of \\cref{obj:def:population-decoder}: whenever \\(H_D\\) contains \\(j\\to k\\), \\(\\tau(j)<\\tau(k)\\).\n\\item \\textbf{(Transported graph order.)} The same order respects the transported latent DAG: whenever \\(\\pi(j)\\to\\pi(k)\\) is an edge of \\(G\\), \\(\\tau(j)<\\tau(k)\\).\n\\end{itemize}\nFix \\(i\\in[n]\\), and put\n\\[\nB_i^\\tau=\\{j\\in[n]:\\tau(j)<\\tau(i)\\}.\n\\]\nFor each predecessor log-ratio vector \\(\\ell\\in\\mathbb R^{B_i^\\tau}\\), let \\(\\kappa_i^\\tau(\\ell,\\cdot)\\) be the law on \\(\\mathbb R\\) of\n\\[\n\\log\\frac{q_{\\pi(i)}(W_i)}{p_{\\pi(i)}\\!\\left(\\widetilde v_i^\\tau(z_i^\\tau(\\ell),W_i)\\right)},\n\\qquad W_i\\sim q_{\\pi(i)}(w)\\,dw \\text{ on }[0,1],\n\\]\nwhere \\(z_i^\\tau=(\\Lambda_i^\\tau)^{-1}\\circ\\rho_i^\\tau\\) is the triangular predecessor-score inverse composed with the retraction onto the realized score range \\(\\mathcal R_i^\\tau\\), and \\(\\widetilde v_i^\\tau(z,w)\\) is the latent point whose \\(\\pi(j)\\)-coordinate is \\(z_j\\) for \\(j\\in B_i^\\tau\\), whose \\(\\pi(i)\\)-coordinate is \\(w\\), and whose remaining coordinates are zero. Then, under the target-\\(\\pi(i)\\) observed environment law \\(P^i\\), the joint law of the predecessor log-ratios and the target log-ratio factorizes as\n\\[\n(L_{B_i^\\tau},L_i)_{\\#}P^i\n=\n(L_{B_i^\\tau})_{\\#}P^i\\otimes \\kappa_i^\\tau .\n\\]",
        "frozen_title": "Kernel factorization of scores"
      },
      "lean": {
        "decl_name": "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.observedRatioPredecessor_compProd",
        "file": "Helpers/DecoderCompProd.lean"
      },
      "review": {
        "status": "matched",
        "passed_hash": "d3ab8e0171c40acc5cf5934b2606d6d8df037ced",
        "note": "Lean's `observedRatioPredecessor_compProd` states that the pushforward of (predecessor log-ratio projection, target log-ratio) under `W.law i.succ` equals the pushforward of the predecessor projection composed (`⊗ₘ`) with `equationElevenAmbientKernel`; that kernel is the retracted score-image kernel whose value at a realized score is the pushforward of the normalized replacement measure along the clamped equation-(11) fiber score, which is the kernel described here."
      },
      "proof": {
        "state": "complete",
        "sorry_count": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "thm:simultaneous-confidence-edges",
      "obj_id": "T-4",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "For arbitrary training-fold estimates \\(\\widehat R_i\\), suppose the simultaneous first-stage event \\(\\{\\max_{i,e}\\mathbb E_{P^e}|\\widehat R_i(X)-R_i(X)|\\le a_N\\}\\) has probability at least \\(1-\\eta\\). Conditional on the training folds and this event, the independent evaluation folds satisfy \\[\\Pr_{\\mathrm{eval}}\\!\\left\\{\\max_{j\\ne i}|\\widehat D_{ji}-D_{ji}|\\le\\varepsilon_N(\\alpha,\\eta)\\right\\}\\ge1-\\alpha.\\] Consequently the same simultaneous bound has unconditional probability at least \\(1-\\alpha-\\eta\\). Every edge of \\(\\widehat H\\) is a true ancestral relation in \\(G^\\pi\\); if \\(\\min_{\\pi(j)\\lessdot_G\\pi(i)}D_{ji}>2\\varepsilon_N(\\alpha,\\eta)\\), then \\(\\operatorname{TC}(\\widehat H)=\\operatorname{TC}(G^\\pi)\\).",
        "tex_anchor": "",
        "frozen": true,
        "frozen_body": "Fix \\(n\\ge 1\\), a labeled DAG \\(G\\) on \\([n]\\), a sign vector \\(s\\), a mechanism \\(\\theta\\), an observed world with target permutation \\(\\pi\\), and a sample-split experiment \\(S\\). Suppose:\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item \\textbf{(Structural model.)} The mechanism, shared mixing representation, and one-intervention-per-node design satisfy \\cref{obj:ass:positive-normalized-smooth-mechanisms,obj:ass:shared-diffeomorphic-mixing,obj:ass:one-perfect-intervention-per-node}.\n\\item \\textbf{(Sample splitting.)} The training and evaluation folds satisfy \\cref{obj:ass:independent-environment-sampling}, and each environment has evaluation sample size \\(N_e\\ge 1\\).\n\\item \\textbf{(Levels.)} The familywise evaluation level and first-stage failure level satisfy \\(\\alpha,\\eta\\in(0,1)\\).\n\\item \\textbf{(First-stage event.)} With\n\\[\n\\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{fs}}\n=\n\\left\\{\n\\omega:\n\\forall i\\in[n],\\ \\forall e\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n\\},\\\n\\int\n\\left|\\widehat R_i(x)-R_i(x)\\right|\n\\,dP^e(x)\n\\le a_N(\\eta)\n\\right\\},\n\\]\nwhere the displayed integrals are finite, the training-fold event obeys\n\\[\n\\Pr(\\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{fs}})\\ge 1-\\eta .\n\\]\n\\end{itemize}\nLet \\(\\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{MMD}}\\) be the simultaneous evaluation event\n\\[\n\\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{MMD}}\n=\n\\left\\{\n\\omega:\n\\forall j\\ne i,\\\n\\left|\\widehat D_{ji}(\\omega)-D_{ji}\\right|\n\\le \\varepsilon_N(\\alpha,\\eta)\n\\right\\}.\n\\]\nThen, conditionally on the training fold and on \\(\\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{fs}}\\), this event has probability at least \\(1-\\alpha\\): for every training-fold measurable event \\(B\\),\n\\[\n(1-\\alpha)\\Pr(\\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{fs}}\\cap B)\n\\le\n\\Pr(\\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{MMD}}\\cap\\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{fs}}\\cap B).\n\\]\nConsequently,\n\\[\n\\Pr(\\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{MMD}})\\ge 1-\\alpha-\\eta .\n\\]\nMoreover, for every \\(\\omega\\in\\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{MMD}}\\), every selected arrow \\(j\\to i\\) of the sample-split confidence graph \\(\\widehat H\\) from \\cref{obj:def:sample-split-confidence-graph} satisfies that \\(\\pi(j)\\) is an ancestor of \\(\\pi(i)\\) in \\(G\\). If, in addition,\n\\[\n2\\varepsilon_N(\\alpha,\\eta)<D_{ji}\n\\qquad\n\\text{for every }j,i\\text{ such that }\\pi(j)\\lessdot_G \\pi(i),\n\\]\nthen for every \\(\\omega\\in\\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{MMD}}\\),\n\\[\n\\operatorname{TC}\\!\\left(\\widehat H(\\omega)\\right)\n=\n\\operatorname{TC}\\!\\left(G^\\pi\\right).\n\\]",
        "frozen_title": "Simultaneous confidence edges"
      },
      "lean": {
        "decl_name": "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.simultaneous_confidence_edges",
        "file": "TSimultaneousConfidenceEdges.lean"
      },
      "review": {
        "status": "matched",
        "passed_hash": "388d7586591c872abaa6a69aa00c74a36c78d8fd",
        "note": "After unfolding all referenced definitions, Lean equivalently states the conditional and unconditional simultaneous MMD bounds, eventwise ancestral-edge soundness, and two-radius ancestral-cover margin recovery of the transitive closure. | Both directions check: `firstStageL1Event` = {∀ i,e: |R̂_i−R_i| integrable ∧ ∫|R̂_i−R_i| dP^e ≤ a_N} (the Integrable conjunct is the well-definedness the paper's E_{P^e}|·| presupposes; without it the Bochner integral would default to 0 and make the event trivially true, so it is the faithful — not a strengthened — rendering of max_{i,e}E_{P^e}|R̂_i−R_i|≤a_N), and hfirst is exactly Pr(E_N)≥1−η; `ConditionalProbabilityAtLeast μ (comap trainingFold) E A (1−α)` unfolds to (1−α)μ(A∩B) ≤ μ(E∩A∩B) for every training-measurable B, which (A itself being training-measurable by hSampling's last clause) is exactly Pr(A_N | training folds) ≥ 1−α a.s. on E_N; conjunct 2 is the unconditional 1−α−η; `simultaneousMmdEvent` = ∀ j≠i, |D̂_ji−D_ji| ≤ ε_N with `confidenceRadius` = 2√2·a_N + 2(1+√(2 log(n(n+1)/α)))/√(min_e N_e), matching the core's ε_N verbatim, and empirical/population discrepancies are the ‖μ̂_ij−μ̂_i0‖ / ‖μ_i0−μ_ij‖ Gaussian-kernel embeddings; conjunct 3 = 'every Ĥ-edge is ancestral in G^π' via G.isAncestor(π j, π i) on the event, matching proof_tex (38); conjunct 4 = (∀ π(j)⋖_G π(i): D_ji > 2ε_N) → TransGen Ĥ = TransGen(permutedGraph) = TC(G^π), the ∀-form being equivalent to the paper's min>2ε_N (vacuous both sides when no covers). Extra binders are all sanctioned: hpos/hmix/hone/hSampling are the node's own depends_on assumptions; hn : 1 ≤ n and hN : ∀e, 1 ≤ N_e are exactly the 'well-typed sampling domain' the frozen proof_tex declares for ε_N; hα/hη merely restate SampleSplitWorld.alpha_mem/eta_mem; the structure's ratioFit_pos matches the frozen symbol signature R̂_i : X → (0,∞) and ratioFit measurability is well-definedness, so 'arbitrary training-fold estimates' is not narrowed; the unused implicit {s : SignVector n} is logically inert (SignVector n is inhabited by value ≡ 1) and adds no restriction. File elaborates with no errors or sorry."
      },
      "proof": {
        "state": "complete",
        "sorry_count": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "oeq:generated-rank-frontier",
      "obj_id": "P-12",
      "kind": "definition",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "Assume the first-stage contract \\(\\inf_{\\theta\\in\\Theta^{\\beta}_{G,s}(c,M,K,\\rho)}\\Pr_\\theta\\{\\mathcal E_N^{\\infty}(b_N)\\}\\ge1-\\eta_N\\), and let \\(h_N\\to0\\) satisfy \\(b_N=o(h_N)\\) and \\(\\underline N h_N^{d_\\star}/\\log(\\underline N)\\to\\infty\\). Using the handle \\(\\mathfrak H_{\\mathrm{rank}}\\), can one construct cross-fitted estimators \\(\\widehat U_i\\) such that \\(\\max_{i\\in[n]}\\|\\widehat U_i-U_i\\|_{\\infty,K}=O_{\\Pr,\\Theta^{\\beta}_{G,s}(c,M,K,\\rho)}(r_N)\\), where \\(r_N=h_N^2+\\sqrt{\\log(\\underline N)/(\\underline N h_N^{d_\\star})}+b_N/h_N\\)? When the first-stage log-ratio estimators additionally admit a uniform asymptotically linear representation on \\(K\\), derive the corresponding expansion for \\(\\widehat U_i-U_i\\) that separates threshold crossings, generated-conditioning perturbations, oracle conditional-CDF variance, and smoothing bias, and characterize the weakest sufficient first-stage remainder bound.",
        "tex_anchor": "",
        "frozen": true,
        "frozen_body": "A natural next question is whether the handle \\(\\mathfrak H_{\\mathrm{rank}}\\) yields uniform generated-rank estimators under the following conditions:\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item \\textbf{(First-stage contract.)}\n\\[\n\\inf_{\\theta\\in\\Theta^{\\beta}_{G,s}(c,M,K,\\rho)}\n\\Pr_\\theta\\{\\mathcal E_N^{\\infty}(b_N)\\}\\ge 1-\\eta_N .\n\\]\n\\item \\textbf{(Bandwidth scale.)} The bandwidth \\(h_N\\) satisfies \\(h_N\\to0\\),\n\\[\nb_N=o(h_N),\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n\\frac{\\underline N h_N^{d_\\star}}{\\log(\\underline N)}\\to\\infty .\n\\]\n\\end{itemize}\nThe target is a construction of cross-fitted estimators \\(\\widehat U_i\\) such that\n\\[\n\\max_{i\\in[n]}\\|\\widehat U_i-U_i\\|_{\\infty,K}\n=\nO_{\\Pr,\\Theta^{\\beta}_{G,s}(c,M,K,\\rho)}(r_N),\n\\]\nwhere\n\\[\nr_N\n=\nh_N^2+\n\\sqrt{\\frac{\\log(\\underline N)}{\\underline N h_N^{d_\\star}}}\n+\\frac{b_N}{h_N}.\n\\]\nWhen the first-stage log-ratio estimators additionally admit a uniform asymptotically linear representation on \\(K\\), future work could derive the corresponding expansion for \\(\\widehat U_i-U_i\\), separating threshold crossings, generated-conditioning perturbations, oracle conditional-CDF variance, and smoothing bias, and could characterize the weakest sufficient first-stage remainder bound.",
        "frozen_title": "Generated-rank frontier"
      },
      "lean": {
        "decl_name": "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.generatedRankFrontierQuestion",
        "file": "Helpers/OpenQuestions.lean"
      },
      "review": {
        "status": "matched",
        "passed_hash": "6c858d58f53553a3ba02b847489f84fc8d60acc4",
        "note": "The closed descriptive payload preserves the full regime, first-stage and bandwidth conditions, proposed uniform rate, requested four-part expansion, weakest-remainder question, and explicit nonassertion of the undefined construction and sharpness; it has no delivered-theorem consumer."
      },
      "proof": {
        "state": "complete",
        "sorry_count": 0
