      "id": "lem:bounded-rkhs-empirical-mean",
      "obj_id": "L-2",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "provenance": "from-note",
      "nl": {
        "statement": "Conditional on the training folds, let \\(X_{e1},\\ldots,X_{eN_e}\\) be the independent evaluation sample from \\(P^e\\), let \\(\\mathcal H_k\\) be the reproducing-kernel Hilbert space of \\(k\\), and put \\(\\phi(a)=k(a,\\cdot)\\).  For \\(n\\ge1\\), with conditional probability at least \\(1-\\alpha\\), simultaneously for every \\(i\\in[n]\\) and \\(e\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n\\}\\),\n\\[\n \\left\\|\\frac1{N_e}\\sum_{r=1}^{N_e}\\phi(\\widehat R_i(X_{er}))\n -\\mathbb E_{P^e}\\phi(\\widehat R_i(X))\\right\\|_{\\mathcal H_k}\n \\le\n \\frac{1+\\sqrt{2\\log\\{n(n+1)/\\alpha\\}}}{\\sqrt{\\min_{0\\le a\\le n}N_a}}.\n\\]",
        "tex_anchor": "",
        "frozen": true,
        "frozen_body": "Fix \\(n\\ge 1\\), a labeled DAG \\(G\\) on \\([n]\\), a mechanism \\(\\theta\\), an observed world with environment laws \\(P^0,\\ldots,P^n\\), and a sample-split experiment \\(S\\). Let \\(\\mathcal H_k\\) be a complete real Hilbert space equipped with a measurable unit-norm feature map \\(\\phi\\) for the Gaussian kernel \\(k(a,b)=\\exp(-(a-b)^2)\\).\n\nAssume:\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item \\textbf{(Conditional evaluation sampling.)} The experiment satisfies the conditional evaluation-sampling conditions: the ambient and environment laws are probability measures; the complete training fold is measurable; the evaluation observations are measurable, independent within each environment, distributed according to their corresponding \\(P^e\\), and independent of the training fold; and the fitted ratio map is jointly measurable in the training fold and the evaluation point.\n\\item \\textbf{(Evaluation sizes.)} Each environment has at least one evaluation observation, \\(N_e\\ge 1\\) for every \\(e\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n\\}\\). Write\n\\[\n\\underline N=\\min_{0\\le e\\le n}N_e .\n\\]\n\\item \\textbf{(Familywise level.)} The error level satisfies \\(\\alpha\\in(0,1)\\).\n\\end{itemize}\n\nFor each training realization, let \\(\\widehat R_i\\) denote the fitted ratio obtained from the complete training fold, and define\n\\[\n\\widehat \\mu_{e i}\n=\n\\frac{1}{N_e}\\sum_{r=1}^{N_e}\\phi\\!\\left(\\widehat R_i(X_{er})\\right),\n\\qquad\n\\mu_{e i}\n=\n\\mathbb E_{X\\sim P^e}\\!\\left[\\phi\\!\\left(\\widehat R_i(X)\\right)\\right].\n\\]\nThen, conditionally on the complete training fold, the simultaneous event\n\\[\n\\forall i\\in[n]\\ \\forall e\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n\\},\\qquad\n\\left\\|\\widehat \\mu_{e i}-\\mu_{e i}\\right\\|_{\\mathcal H_k}\n\\le\n\\frac{1+\\sqrt{2\\log\\!\\left(n(n+1)/\\alpha\\right)}}{\\sqrt{\\underline N}}\n\\]\nhas probability at least \\(1-\\alpha\\). Equivalently, for every event \\(B\\) measurable with respect to the complete training fold,\n\\[\n(1-\\alpha)\\mathbb P(B)\n\\le\n\\mathbb P\\!\\left(\nB\\cap\n\\left\\{\n\\forall i\\in[n]\\ \\forall e\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n\\},\\\n\\left\\|\\widehat \\mu_{e i}-\\mu_{e i}\\right\\|_{\\mathcal H_k}\n\\le\n\\frac{1+\\sqrt{2\\log\\!\\left(n(n+1)/\\alpha\\right)}}{\\sqrt{\\underline N}}\n\\right\\}\n\\right).\n\\]",
        "frozen_title": "Conditional RKHS mean bound"
      },
      "lean": {
        "decl_name": "CausalSmith.ExactID.EID_CrlCoverratioMmdGenericity.bounded_rkhs_empirical_mean",
        "file": "Helpers/RkhsEmpiricalMean.lean"
      },
      "review": {
        "status": "matched",
        "passed_hash": "0a613c73dca8531860644299601b5be7ab993b32",
        "note": "After unfolding the sampling, feature-map, embedding, minimum-size, and conditional-probability definitions, Lean states the same simultaneous n(n+1)-pair conditional deviation bound for conditionally independent evaluation samples from each P^e."
      },
      "proof": {
        "state": "complete",
        "sorry_count": 0
      }
    },
