        "note": "The three structure fields are exactly the stated positivity/normalization/smoothness, causal-minimality, and fixed-sign conditions; the ambient Mechanism topology is induced by its value, first-derivative, and second-derivative coordinates, and StratumPoint inherits the corresponding relative topology."
      },
      "claude": {
        "verdict": "matched",
        "evidence_hash": "0bbf2b92b877476948fad496753253498b1b9040",
        "note": "`ModelStratum` conjoins exactly the three cited assumptions (PositiveNormalizedSmoothMechanisms, CausalMinimality, FixedOwnDerivativeSign) and `StratumPoint` is the subtype over `Mechanism n G`, whose `TopologicalSpace` instance (Basic.lean:49-61) is induced by uniform convergence of p_i, q_i and their first/second within-derivatives on the closed cube / [0,1] — i.e. the relative product C² topology; the extra `parent_local` carrier field is a proof-irrelevant restatement of `p_i` being the conditional density on pa_G(i), so both inclusions hold."
      }
    },
    "def:edge-separated-set": {
      "codex": {
