        "note": "`∀ ⦃j i⦄, G.edge j i → ¬ CondIndepCoordinates θ {i} {j} ((G.parents i).erase j)` unfolds to the negation of `CondIndepFun` of the coordinate projections onto V_i and V_j given σ(V_{pa_G(i)\\{j}}) under `observationalLaw θ`, i.e. exactly the note's 'p⁰ does not satisfy V_i ⊥ V_j | V_{pa_G(i)\\{j}}' for every edge; the `∃ hμ : IsFiniteMeasure`/`∃ _hX,_hY,hZ : Measurable` wrappers inside `CondIndepCoordinates` are the standard Lean idiom for supplying `CondIndepFun`'s instance and measurability arguments — the projection measurability holds unconditionally and the finiteness holds for every mechanism in the paper's class (ass:positive-normalized-smooth-mechanisms makes p⁰ a probability density on the cube, and that assumption accompanies CausalMinimality at every use, including inside ModelStratum), so the two propositions are equivalent on the stated domain."
